message: "If you use these results or this code, please cite it as below."
type: software
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX  (uncomment once the Zenodo DOI is reserved)
title: "How accurate is altitude from pressure geolocators? A global validation of GeoPressureR altitude against station barometers and radiosondes"
abstract: >-
  Validation of the altitude that GeoPressureR and GeoPressureAPI retrieve from a pressure
  measurement using ERA5 reanalysis, against HadISD surface station barometers, GNSS and
  MeteoSwiss stations with documented barometer heights (ground level), and IGRA2 radiosondes
  (0-6 km above ground). Separates accuracy (per-site bias) from precision (temporal scatter),
  shows what they depend on, compares ERA5 single-levels with ERA5-Land, and tests improvements
  of the pressure-to-altitude formula.
